=3 Notes
* Kelp Pugil are very weak and can be killed solo or duo with ease.
* Kelp Pugil do not respawn.
* Movement speed seems to negatively affect interactions with the Apkallu. It is suggested that you remove all forms of movement speed + for this assault.

=2 Walkthrough
To win this assault, herd 1 or more {n:Fairy Apkallu} to {n:Clavauert B Chanoix} for his {p:Lebros Apkallu Brothel|Apkallu Breeding}.
In order to herd a {n:Fairy Apkallu}, a complicated courting process must be followed:
* First, obtain a {i:Hamsi|Hamsi|5449} by finding and clicking on one of the many ??? that are scattered about the map.
* Once you have a delicious fish, find a passive {n:Fairy Apkallu}. Stand in front of it at a medium-short distance, close enough to select the target.

* The Apkallu will stop and stare at you, and you will receive the message "The Fairy Apkallu is staring at you"
* **/bow** to the Apkallu.
** One of two things will happen:
*** "The Fairy Apkallu is wary of your presence"; repeat the process again.
*** "The Fairy Apkallu seems curious about you"; repeat the process again.
* If you receive the message that the Apkallu "let down its guard", immediately use the **/welcome** motion.
** If the Apkallu says it likes you, you then have __one second__ to click the Apkallu to give it the {i:Hamsi|Hamsi|5449}.
*** If done successfully, you will get the message "You successfully capture the Fairy Apkallu!". When this happens, **quickly circle directly behind the Apkallu,** and stand about 3 Yalms away directly **behind** the Fairy Apkallu.
*** **NOTE**: Apkallu's that "liked" you will not give this message again for the duration of the assault. It will keep saying "It's wary of you" but you can keep giving it Hamsi until the **captured** mode. In other words, you can't feed Hamsi to an Apkallu until it has been allowed after the first "it likes you" message, then it can be fed Hamsi anytime when it stares at you. You will not get another "it likes you" message if you try to redo the **/bow** and **/welcome** reactions because it already likes you to begin with (Useful if you failed to /welcome quick enough or this Apkallu ran away and are attempting to recapture).
* The Fairy Apkallu will slowly waddle towards the Professor. Stay a few yalms directly behind the Fairy Apkallu. If it turns, as it will near the Professor, make sure you adjust to stay directly behind it. Be careful of cliffs; the Apkallu will go straight up while you will need to quickly navigate the cliff.
* If the Fairy Apkallu sees any Kelp Pugil, it will flee. If you are quick, you can immediately recapture it sometimes by running behind it and clicking it again.
* If you leave the "safe zone" behind the Apkallu, it will stop. If you do not return quickly to the position behind the Apkallu, it will run away and the courting process will need to be repeated.
** You will need to click another ??? for a new {i:Hamsi|Hamsi|5449} if it runs away.

* **DO NOT GO INTO FIRST-PERSON MODE!** There are two hills next to the start quest NPC that require third-person mode in order to traverse if approaching from the left-hand side (if looking at the NPC). Far better strategy is to just lock on the Apkallu and position your self accordingly and when you have to run around terrain; unlock , run around terrain, re-lock, and reposition.

Herding a single {n:Fairy Apkallu} will cause the {p:Rune of Release} to spawn at the professor. Capturing more Apkallu will increase the amount of points earned, to a maximum of 1333 with 3 people.
